                <pb facs="0564" n="484" sameAs="frus:frus1936v01/pg484"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">500.C1112/86: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Secretary of State to the Consul at
                        Geneva</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Gilbert</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1936-12-30T17:00:00-05:00">December 30,
                            1936—5 p.m.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>162. Your 520, December 17, 4 p.m. We are considering suggesting the same person
                    for membership on the Economic and Raw Materials Committees. As apparently the
                    Raw Materials Committee is to be composed largely of members of the Economic
                    Committee we presume that meetings of the two bodies will be coordinated.
                    However, we desire any information you may be able promptly to secure concerning
                    such coordination and concerning the probable frequency, dates and duration of
                    meetings of the Raw Materials Committee.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Moore</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
